url: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/LLM-ACCEL"
license: "PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  LLM-ACCEL is a synthesizable HLS and RTL hardware-emulation research
  prototype that separates model-aware decoder scheduling and memory state
  from two regular stream-only 8x64 compute arrays. It explores block-level
  streaming, host-composed controller-resident subgraphs, 1--8-row block
  prefill, online attention, resident KV-cache management, and cross-wave
  load/compute/collect overlap for Qwen-style decoder layers.
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - large language model
  - transformer accelerator
  - high-level synthesis
  - streaming architecture
  - online attention
